2149
00:03:08,397 --> 00:03:09,727
I don’t get it.

2150
00:03:09,827 --> 00:03:11,527
How do you explain that?

2151
00:03:11,527 --> 00:03:13,667
Hello, hello!

2152
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:15,167
And thanks for joining us again!

2153
00:03:15,167 --> 00:03:16,307
Now, let’s get ready to…

2154
00:03:16,307 --> 00:03:17,697
Q, Q, Q!

2155
00:03:19,877 --> 00:03:23,407
That’s right.
I’m your host, MCQ.

2156
00:03:23,407 --> 00:03:25,407
Thank you.
P-p-pleez!

2157
00:03:25,407 --> 00:03:27,347
You’re tired of seeing my face?

2158
00:03:27,347 --> 00:03:29,747
No, don’t say that.
You’re horrible!

2159
00:03:30,947 --> 00:03:32,647
Oh, it’s time?

2160
00:03:32,647 --> 00:03:37,147
Then as usual, we’ll start off
by explaining the show’s rules, Q-Q-Q!

2161
00:03:37,327 --> 00:03:39,627
<i>It’s an incredibly simple quiz show…</i>

2162
00:03:39,627 --> 00:03:42,457
<i>in which the contestant must score
1 million points in 30 minutes.</i>

2163
00:03:42,457 --> 00:03:44,697
<i>If he can answer the
various questions correctly and…</i>

2164
00:03:44,697 --> 00:03:46,697
<i>reach the magic
1 million point mark…</i>

2165
00:03:46,697 --> 00:03:48,997
<i>these fabulous prizes are all his.</i>

2166
00:03:48,997 --> 00:03:52,137
<i>And as a bonus prize, the moment
he makes it past the 1 million point…</i>

2167
00:03:52,137 --> 00:03:54,937
<i>the show’s host, MCQ, will die.</i>

2168
00:03:54,937 --> 00:03:56,377
That’s right, I’m toast!

2169
00:03:56,377 --> 00:03:58,977
In other words,
the moment the challenger wins…

2170
00:03:58,977 --> 00:04:00,677
the show is over!

2171
00:04:00,677 --> 00:04:03,487
Challenger: 0 victories
MCQ: 25 victories
Somehow I’ve managed to
win 25 times in a row…

2172
00:04:03,487 --> 00:04:06,517
Challenger: 0 victories
MCQ: 25 victories
and a victory today
will make it 2 full seasons.

2173
00:04:06,517 --> 00:04:09,217
I wonder, do you think
I can pull it off again today?!

2174
00:04:09,217 --> 00:04:12,487
So, what happens if our contestant
doesn’t reach 1 million points?

2175
00:04:12,487 --> 00:04:15,727
Let’s hear you explain it
while gradually getting older.

2176
00:04:15,727 --> 00:04:16,127
Challenger: LOSE
MCQ: WIN

2177
00:04:16,127 --> 00:04:18,597
Challenger: LOSE
MCQ: WIN
<i>If they don’t reach
1 million points…</i>

2178
00:04:18,597 --> 00:04:21,237
Challenger: LOSE
MCQ: WIN
<i>then I’m afraid
the challenger dies.</i>

2179
00:04:21,237 --> 00:04:24,707
Challenger: LOSE
MCQ: WIN
<i>So answer as best you can and
hopefully you won’t die, all right?</i>

2180
00:04:24,707 --> 00:04:28,277
I just love hearing you ad-lib
that part each week, Somi!

2181
00:04:28,277 --> 00:04:30,477
All right, let’s get started!

2182
00:04:30,477 --> 00:04:33,477
Nightmare Quiz Show!
1 million points…

2183
00:04:33,477 --> 00:04:35,037
in 30 minutes!

2184
00:04:36,247 --> 00:04:40,487
Nightmare Quiz Show
1 million points in 30 minutes

2185
00:04:40,487 --> 00:04:43,947
LIVE
Nightmare Quiz Show
1 million points in 30 minutes

2186
00:04:50,967 --> 00:04:53,167
Let’s introduce him once again.

2187
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,697
Who is today’s challenger…

2188
00:04:54,697 --> 00:04:57,537
this man appearing
out of the freezing heartland?

2189
00:04:57,537 --> 00:05:00,437
<i>He’s Vincent Law,
who comes to us from Romdeau City.</i>

2190
00:05:00,637 --> 00:05:02,797
Vincent Law

2191
00:05:03,477 --> 00:05:06,347
Romdeau? You’ve come
quite a distance to be here with us.

2192
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:07,117
So, what’s up?

2193
00:05:07,117 --> 00:05:08,447
What’s up with what?

2194
00:05:08,447 --> 00:05:10,477
We’re not clicking, are we?
Well, that’s OK.

2195
00:05:10,947 --> 00:05:12,487
Occupation…

2196
00:05:12,487 --> 00:05:15,177
says here you’re currently
unemployed with no fixed address.

2197
00:05:16,017 --> 00:05:18,027
Looks like things haven’t
been going your way.

2198
00:05:18,027 --> 00:05:19,957
Not much meat
on your bones either.

2199
00:05:19,957 --> 00:05:22,057
Well, that’s how it is these days.

2200
00:05:22,057 --> 00:05:24,497
No one said life was easy.

2201
00:05:24,497 --> 00:05:28,497
But the only thing standing
between you and me is this program.

2202
00:05:28,497 --> 00:05:31,667
This could be your chance to
get all those fabulous prizes.

2203
00:05:31,667 --> 00:05:33,197
Uh… sure…

2204
00:05:33,507 --> 00:05:35,197
How many points
does he currently have?

2205
00:05:35,707 --> 00:05:37,977
<i>He has 90,000 points
with 3 correct answers.</i>

2206
00:05:38,177 --> 00:05:41,517
We’re not off to a
very good start, are we?

2207
00:05:41,517 --> 00:05:42,817
Are you gonna be OK?

2208
00:05:42,817 --> 00:05:44,287
Uh… yeah…

2209
00:05:44,287 --> 00:05:46,977
Not one for words, is he?

2210
00:05:47,357 --> 00:05:49,977
Is he nervous?
Maybe he knows something we don’t.

2211
00:05:50,387 --> 00:05:53,527
Even this unemployed man
with no fixed address has 2 friends…

2212
00:05:53,527 --> 00:05:57,727
who’ve come to cheer him on
from our supporter boxes.

2213
00:05:58,027 --> 00:06:02,267
Supporter Box
I don’t know what they’re saying,
but you feel their spirit, don’t you?

2214
00:06:03,207 --> 00:06:05,967
<i>In addition,
as always during the program…</i>

2215
00:06:05,967 --> 00:06:08,437
<i>there will be a
</i><i>“Catch the Mistake Quiz” for you.</i>

2216
00:06:08,437 --> 00:06:09,807
<i>So keep an eye out.</i>

2217
00:06:09,807 --> 00:06:11,977
You really never know
when it’s going to pop up.

2218
00:06:11,977 --> 00:06:15,217
People in our studio audience,
keep an eye out as well!

2219
00:06:15,217 --> 00:06:17,737
Who knows,
one of you could be the winner!

2220
00:06:23,427 --> 00:06:24,757
Oh, time to resume!

2221
00:06:24,757 --> 00:06:26,747
Our next quiz is…

2222
00:06:27,427 --> 00:06:30,757
The panel quiz, “Who is it?”
Rules <i>p-p-</i> pleeez!

2223
00:06:31,397 --> 00:06:33,737
<i>Panel Quiz:
“Who is it?”</i>

2224
00:06:33,737 --> 00:06:35,567
<i>In a few moments…</i>

2225
00:06:35,567 --> 00:06:38,107
<i>impressions and images about
a certain person will appear…</i>

2226
00:06:38,107 --> 00:06:40,577
<i>one after another
on the panels of this screen.</i>

2227
00:06:40,577 --> 00:06:42,577
<i>Using these hints as clues…</i>

2228
00:06:42,577 --> 00:06:45,507
<i>please tell us who it is we’re
talking about as soon as you know.</i>

2229
00:06:45,507 --> 00:06:48,037
<i>The sooner you answer,
the more points you get.</i>

2230
00:06:48,247 --> 00:06:49,247
Oh, my!

2231
00:06:49,247 --> 00:06:52,687
If you answer it after the first hint,
you get 600,000 points!

2232
00:06:52,687 --> 00:06:56,847
Each panel that’s turned over thereafter
reduces the amount by 50,000 points.

2233
00:06:57,087 --> 00:06:59,687
Answer correctly after
all the panels have been turned over…

2234
00:06:59,687 --> 00:07:00,827
and you only get 50,000 points.

2235
00:07:00,827 --> 00:07:02,997
Well then,
let’s go ahead and give it a try!

2236
00:07:02,997 --> 00:07:04,297
Who is it?

2237
00:07:07,537 --> 00:07:09,367
It says they like to wear black.

2238
00:07:09,367 --> 00:07:10,907
Is it someone fashionable?

2239
00:07:10,907 --> 00:07:13,037
Or someone who’s
suffered a misfortune?

2240
00:07:13,037 --> 00:07:14,607
I’ll be amazed
if you know just from this.

2241
00:07:14,607 --> 00:07:15,807
Think! Think!

2242
00:07:15,807 --> 00:07:16,867
Black…

2243
00:07:17,777 --> 00:07:19,447
Has a mean look in their eyes.

2244
00:07:19,447 --> 00:07:20,947
Someone in black
with a mean look in their eyes.

2245
00:07:20,947 --> 00:07:24,077
Is it someone scary?
Or maybe they have poor vision?

2246
00:07:24,517 --> 00:07:26,107
Come on, Vincent!
You can do it!

2247
00:07:27,117 --> 00:07:30,057
Appears to be young,
but they’re older than they look.

2248
00:07:30,757 --> 00:07:31,627
He’s ready to answer!

2249
00:07:31,627 --> 00:07:33,557
Let’s hear it, shall we?

2250
00:07:33,557 --> 00:07:36,087
If he answers right,
he’ll get a whopping 450,000 points.

2251
00:07:36,627 --> 00:07:38,927
He’s smiling!
He seems confident.

2252
00:07:39,467 --> 00:07:41,997
Let’s hear your answer.
Who is it?

2253
00:07:41,997 --> 00:07:43,197
Re-l Mayer!

2254
00:07:45,167 --> 00:07:47,577
Someone who likes to wear black,
has a mean look in their eyes…

2255
00:07:47,577 --> 00:07:48,677
and is older than they appear.

2256
00:07:48,677 --> 00:07:51,747
And he thought it was Re-l Mayer.

2257
00:07:51,747 --> 00:07:54,547
I’m sorry!
Not even close.

2258
00:07:54,547 --> 00:07:56,347
Hey, Re-l Mayer
in the supporters box…

2259
00:07:56,347 --> 00:07:59,217
Vincent says you try to make yourself
look younger than you really are!

2260
00:07:59,617 --> 00:08:00,417
Re-l Mayer

2261
00:08:00,417 --> 00:08:02,587
Very well.
Back to the quiz.

2262
00:08:02,587 --> 00:08:05,027
The studio audience
is coming alive!

2263
00:08:05,027 --> 00:08:06,487
Who is it?

2264
00:08:09,597 --> 00:08:11,227
Able to withstand the cold.

2265
00:08:11,527 --> 00:08:13,597
I wonder how they do in the heat.

2266
00:08:13,597 --> 00:08:15,497
Is it simply someone
with endurance?

2267
00:08:17,107 --> 00:08:18,227
Shy with strangers.

2268
00:08:19,137 --> 00:08:21,577
It’s someone who doesn’t engage in
conversation when you first meet them.

2269
00:08:21,577 --> 00:08:23,707
It takes time for them
to feel at home…

2270
00:08:23,707 --> 00:08:25,977
but once they do, perhaps
they start acting a little too familiar.

2271
00:08:27,117 --> 00:08:29,407
They’ve got their eye on Vincent.

2272
00:08:29,847 --> 00:08:32,817
My goodness.
That’s a huge hint, isn’t it?

2273
00:08:33,117 --> 00:08:37,147
Could that mean
it’s someone you know?

2274
00:08:37,727 --> 00:08:41,757
Yes, Vincent.
Answer correctly for 350,000 points.

2275
00:08:41,757 --> 00:08:44,567
Who is it
that has their mind on you?

2276
00:08:44,567 --> 00:08:45,257
Pino!

2277
00:08:47,697 --> 00:08:49,067
Pino

2278
00:08:49,067 --> 00:08:51,807
I mean, when you said
“able to withstand cold…”

2279
00:08:51,807 --> 00:08:54,097
the only one I could think of
was the AutoReiv.

2280
00:08:54,337 --> 00:08:55,807
But, look there.
See!

2281
00:08:56,337 --> 00:08:59,037
You call that a
mean look in her eyes?

2282
00:08:59,677 --> 00:09:01,317
You look like you’ve hit upon something.
Yes. Yes!

2283
00:09:01,317 --> 00:09:03,787
You’ve got to think of
everything together…

2284
00:09:03,787 --> 00:09:06,587
including the fact they like to
wear black and appear to be young!

2285
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:09,017
I mean, is there some benefit
for a guy to act like an airhead?

2286
00:09:09,017 --> 00:09:10,887
If there is,
maybe I’ll give it a try.

2287
00:09:10,887 --> 00:09:12,427
No… I mean…

2288
00:09:12,427 --> 00:09:14,357
Well then, Mr. Airhead,
let’s see…

2289
00:09:14,357 --> 00:09:16,057
Who is it?

2290
00:09:19,067 --> 00:09:20,337
Keeps mouth shut…

2291
00:09:20,337 --> 00:09:22,167
They don’t just
keep their mouth shut…

2292
00:09:22,167 --> 00:09:24,797
they keep it shut for a reason.
It’s something that serves them well.

2293
00:09:25,007 --> 00:09:27,037
Tears…
keeps their mouth shut…

2294
00:09:27,037 --> 00:09:28,697
Surprisingly prone to tears.

2295
00:09:28,907 --> 00:09:31,447
Interesting.
It’s coming to you now, isn’t it?

2296
00:09:31,447 --> 00:09:33,437
Prone to tears.
That seems like a great hint!

2297
00:09:34,647 --> 00:09:36,247
Likely has a hidden side.

2298
00:09:36,247 --> 00:09:38,247
Well, that would certainly
appear to be the case.

2299
00:09:38,247 --> 00:09:39,717
I get the feeling this is someone…

2300
00:09:39,717 --> 00:09:41,687
who manipulates things
from behind the scenes.

2301
00:09:42,187 --> 00:09:43,217
Winner…

2302
00:09:43,217 --> 00:09:44,857
The sole winner!

2303
00:09:44,857 --> 00:09:47,697
You must know by now, don’t you?
You’re almost out of time.

2304
00:09:47,697 --> 00:09:50,667
Here, it’s on the tip of your tongue,
Pr…

2305
00:09:50,667 --> 00:09:51,357
Pr?

2306
00:09:52,767 --> 00:09:54,267
Naked under blue skies.

2307
00:09:54,267 --> 00:09:57,307
I don’t know about anyone naked,
but have you ever seen a blue sky?

2308
00:09:57,307 --> 00:10:00,237
Naked under blue skies.
Blue skies over them naked!

2309
00:10:00,477 --> 00:10:01,337
Here it is!

2310
00:10:01,577 --> 00:10:02,977
Once and for all,
who is it?!

2311
00:10:03,607 --> 00:10:05,737
Which is to say,
this is your last chance!

2312
00:10:06,107 --> 00:10:08,177
Likes to wear black.
Has a mean look in their eyes.

2313
00:10:08,177 --> 00:10:10,287
Appears to be young.
Able to withstand cold.

2314
00:10:10,287 --> 00:10:13,617
Shy with strangers.
They’ve got Vincent on their mind.

2315
00:10:13,617 --> 00:10:16,157
A person prone to tears.
Keeps their mouth shut for a reason.

2316
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:17,527
Likely to have a hidden side.

2317
00:10:17,527 --> 00:10:22,327
Even so, they’re the sole winner
who’s naked under blue skies.

2318
00:10:22,327 --> 00:10:24,567
The person who
looks like this is who?!

2319
00:10:24,567 --> 00:10:26,687
Ergo Proxy!

2320
00:10:28,897 --> 00:10:30,907
Nice try.
Nice try.

2321
00:10:30,907 --> 00:10:32,707
Close but no cigar.

2322
00:10:32,707 --> 00:10:33,767
The correct answer is…

2323
00:10:34,577 --> 00:10:36,577
<i>The correct answer is
Proxy One.</i>

2324
00:10:36,577 --> 00:10:38,477
Huh? Who?

2325
00:10:38,947 --> 00:10:42,247
I’m afraid you got
shut out in this round!

2326
00:10:45,247 --> 00:10:47,417
Well, moving right along!

2327
00:10:47,417 --> 00:10:50,787
It’s time for the Mosaic Quiz,
“What’s it making?”

2328
00:10:52,387 --> 00:10:55,557
<i>Mosaic Quiz:
“What’s This a Picture Of?”</i>

2329
00:10:55,557 --> 00:11:00,867
<i>In a moment, a pixilated image
will appear on the monitor.</i>

2330
00:11:00,867 --> 00:11:02,367
<i>Using the pixilated image as a clue…</i>

2331
00:11:02,367 --> 00:11:06,107
<i>please tell us what it’s making
as soon as you know.</i>

2332
00:11:06,107 --> 00:11:09,127
<i>A correct answer will
earn you 200,000 points.</i>

2333
00:11:09,337 --> 00:11:12,107
All right, shall we?
Starting with the following image.

2334
00:11:12,107 --> 00:11:15,637
What’s it making?
Q, Q, Q we go!

2335
00:11:16,077 --> 00:11:18,147
Huh? Um…

2336
00:11:18,147 --> 00:11:19,817
I can’t tell at all from this.

2337
00:11:19,817 --> 00:11:21,117
Oh, really?

2338
00:11:21,757 --> 00:11:25,587
Why don’t you try squinting?
Maybe that’ll help.

2339
00:11:25,957 --> 00:11:27,127
It’s there.
It’s there.

2340
00:11:27,127 --> 00:11:29,227
Perhaps it’s something
you recognize from before.

2341
00:11:29,227 --> 00:11:31,657
Look!
There’s something moving.

2342
00:11:31,967 --> 00:11:33,797
It’s some type of blob.

2343
00:11:33,797 --> 00:11:36,197
But see,
it’s getting bigger.

2344
00:11:36,197 --> 00:11:38,537
That’s right.
It’s something that’s being bred.

2345
00:11:38,537 --> 00:11:40,807
Something that moves
and grows…

2346
00:11:40,807 --> 00:11:41,877
so it’s alive!

2347
00:11:41,877 --> 00:11:42,707
Alive…

2348
00:11:42,707 --> 00:11:44,507
Yes, yes.
Although not quite.

2349
00:11:44,507 --> 00:11:46,917
I don’t want to give it away,
but it’s not really alive.

2350
00:11:46,917 --> 00:11:49,017
It looks like it’s alive,
but it’s a little different.

2351
00:11:49,017 --> 00:11:50,047
Looks like it’s alive…

2352
00:11:50,047 --> 00:11:53,217
but that wasn’t necessarily
anyone’s fault.

2353
00:11:53,217 --> 00:11:56,417
Since they couldn’t
foresee the cause either.

2354
00:11:56,417 --> 00:12:00,057
See, it took longer for the planet’s
environment to restore itself…

2355
00:12:00,057 --> 00:12:02,887
than the creators
had expected, right?

2356
00:12:03,567 --> 00:12:06,727
That’s probably why
their calculations got all messed up.

2357
00:12:06,727 --> 00:12:10,107
So in the meantime,
they needed a dome, right?

2358
00:12:10,107 --> 00:12:11,567
Hey, I just gave you a big hint!

2359
00:12:11,567 --> 00:12:12,807
What’s it making?

2360
00:12:12,807 --> 00:12:13,707
A human being!

2361
00:12:17,447 --> 00:12:19,977
Again, nice try.
You’re so close!

2362
00:12:19,977 --> 00:12:22,447
A person! Humanity!
Man! Woman!

2363
00:12:23,347 --> 00:12:24,787
Good guesses,
but not quite.

2364
00:12:24,787 --> 00:12:27,947
Before we give the answer,
it’s time for a short break.

2365
00:12:37,997 --> 00:12:41,537
<i>The plan went into effect in a much
harsher “Awakening Environment…”</i>

2366
00:12:41,537 --> 00:12:44,027
<i>than had been anticipated.</i>

2367
00:12:44,637 --> 00:12:48,977
<i>What proved to be the undoing for the
creators under these harsh conditions…</i>

2368
00:12:48,977 --> 00:12:53,637
was the overabundance of data carefully
preserved as the “Origin of the Species.”

2369
00:12:54,147 --> 00:12:58,787
<i>In these cities, the ability to adapt to a
</i><i>changing environment was unnecessary.</i>

2370
00:12:58,787 --> 00:13:01,917
<i>Therefore, despite the fact
they were produced through…</i>

2371
00:13:01,917 --> 00:13:04,287
It’s a mysterious radio wave
of unknown origin.

2372
00:13:04,287 --> 00:13:06,857
An analysis of its source
confirmed that…

2373
00:13:06,857 --> 00:13:09,557
it was being transmitted
via satellite.

2374
00:13:10,467 --> 00:13:14,527
They even launched a satellite
just so they could show this?

2375
00:13:15,267 --> 00:13:18,067
We’re currently cooperating
with various departments…

2376
00:13:18,067 --> 00:13:20,337
as we continue to check
the dome’s jamming system…

2377
00:13:20,337 --> 00:13:22,907
for blocking outside information.

2378
00:13:22,907 --> 00:13:23,807
<i>The creators were also
considered to be failures.</i>

2379
00:13:23,807 --> 00:13:24,907
<i>The creators were also
considered to be failures.</i>
Re-l…

2380
00:13:24,907 --> 00:13:25,377
<i>The creators were also
considered to be failures.</i>

2381
00:13:25,377 --> 00:13:31,147
<i>The ones who admired such failures
as creators were failures themselves.</i>

2382
00:13:31,147 --> 00:13:32,637
<i>The ones who admired such failures
as creators were failures themselves.</i>
Vincent Law.

2383
00:13:35,857 --> 00:13:37,987
<i>Moving on!
It’s “Triple Chance”!</i>

2384
00:13:37,987 --> 00:13:40,497
<i>For this quiz,
all point values are tripled!</i>

2385
00:13:40,497 --> 00:13:43,697
<i>And for no particular reason,
we’ll have 3 contestants!</i>

2386
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,367
Over here!

2387
00:13:45,367 --> 00:13:47,597
All right,
good luck you three!

2388
00:13:47,767 --> 00:13:49,567
Vincent, what is this idiocy?!

2389
00:13:49,567 --> 00:13:52,397
Hey look, young lady,
the cue card says we’re moving on.

2390
00:13:55,537 --> 00:13:57,207
Well, back to the quiz.

2391
00:13:57,207 --> 00:13:59,847
First, please watch the video.

2392
00:13:59,847 --> 00:14:01,277
Q, Q, Q, we go!

2393
00:14:04,047 --> 00:14:05,677
<i>History of the Earth.</i>

2394
00:14:06,247 --> 00:14:09,717
<i>Billions of years after the
universe was created in the Big Bang…</i>

2395
00:14:09,717 --> 00:14:14,197
<i>a strange planet is born on the
edge of an ordinary galaxy.</i>

2396
00:14:14,197 --> 00:14:15,817
<i>The name of the planet…
Earth.</i>

2397
00:14:16,557 --> 00:14:19,427
<i>Before long, a miraculous ocean
comes into existence.</i>

2398
00:14:19,997 --> 00:14:22,237
<i>Seaweed and fish all pressing up
against each other.</i>

2399
00:14:22,237 --> 00:14:24,507
<i>Many things happen over the
next few hundred million years.</i>

2400
00:14:24,507 --> 00:14:26,237
<i>On land, dinosaurs
come into existence.</i>

2401
00:14:26,237 --> 00:14:28,107
<i>It’s the law of the jungle.</i>

2402
00:14:28,107 --> 00:14:30,307
<i>Eat, be eaten,
or try to get away.</i>

2403
00:14:30,307 --> 00:14:35,037
<i>Now we come to the age of mammals.
Our ancestors are born.</i>

2404
00:14:35,677 --> 00:14:37,687
<i>In order to catch
their prey by chance…</i>

2405
00:14:37,687 --> 00:14:40,947
<i>one of them raises
the bone they’re holding.</i>

2406
00:14:41,517 --> 00:14:45,127
<i>Yes. This is the moment when the
first tool comes into existence.</i>

2407
00:14:45,127 --> 00:14:46,757
<i>Way to go humans!</i>

2408
00:14:46,757 --> 00:14:48,097
Amazing!

2409
00:14:48,097 --> 00:14:51,427
Well, while keeping this
“History of the Earth” in mind…

2410
00:14:51,427 --> 00:14:54,267
write your answers down on the
boards you have there in your hands.

2411
00:14:54,267 --> 00:14:58,007
OK, Mosaic Quiz.
What’s it making?

2412
00:14:58,007 --> 00:14:59,497
Q-Q-Q we go!

2413
00:14:59,807 --> 00:15:02,937
It’s related to the bone
the monkey was holding.

2414
00:15:02,937 --> 00:15:05,307
Yes, start thinking.
It’s thinking time!

2415
00:15:05,577 --> 00:15:06,147
The bone?

2416
00:15:06,147 --> 00:15:08,547
That’s right.
Tool evolution.

2417
00:15:08,547 --> 00:15:12,077
You’re going in the right direction.
It’s the last big one they made.

2418
00:15:12,587 --> 00:15:15,617
But they had to rush, so not everyone
could fit, and it was useless.

2419
00:15:15,617 --> 00:15:18,587
In that sense,
it created widespread resentment.

2420
00:15:18,887 --> 00:15:20,797
You should know what it is, right?

2421
00:15:20,797 --> 00:15:22,797
What am I gonna do?
Here’s a big hint!

2422
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:25,527
Come on,
they used it to try to get away!

2423
00:15:26,297 --> 00:15:29,797
All right!
Thinking time is over.

2424
00:15:29,797 --> 00:15:32,037
Shall we go ahead
and take a look?

2425
00:15:32,037 --> 00:15:33,467
First, young lady…

2426
00:15:33,467 --> 00:15:34,267
Ta-da!

2427
00:15:34,937 --> 00:15:36,837
You drew the pixilated image,
did you?

2428
00:15:36,837 --> 00:15:38,877
That’s a lot of squares.

2429
00:15:38,877 --> 00:15:40,537
Next, Miss Mayer.

